{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>When I break for you the staff of bread.</b> Corresponding to 'your bread to satisfaction,' and it is the fifth. And they restored 'your bread' in the weight of the bet with pataḥ — in the weight of 'bring it to the oven' (הַבִּיאֻהוּ לַתַּנּוּר) and in the weight of 'restore it' (יָשִׁיבֻהוּ), to feed it to the owners with restriction — bread scant and water oppressed, and so it says: 'Behold, I will break the staff of bread in Jerusalem, and they shall eat bread by weight' (Ezekiel 4:16) — and it corresponds to 'because of the new moon you shall bring out,' and it is the sixth." "<b>And you shall eat and not be satisfied.</b> Corresponding to 'and you shall eat old, aged produce,' and it is the seventh."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:36.632370713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}